<opsproc code="00008910.0001001" revdate="2010-03-11T14:31:32"><title>Exterior Crew Oxygen Overpressure Indicator Disc (Green Disc)</title><procitem layer="1" lid="N.00008910.0001001.004"><title>During cockpit preparation</title><procbody lid="N.00008910.0001001.006"><inform layer="1" lid="N.00008910.0001001.007"><para code="00008910.0001001.002" layer="1" lid="N.00008910.0001001.008"><emph bold="false" italic="false" overline="false" sub="false" sup="false" underline="true">Before the first flight of each day, check that the oxygen pressure
does not decrease:</emph></para></inform><relevant-sub-proc lid="N.00008910.0001001.009"><action layer="1" lid="N.00008910.0001001.010" memory="false"><command code="00008910.0001001.003"><para layer="1" lid="N.00008910.0001001.011">On the <tech-label type="s-page">DOOR/OXY</tech-label>, check the OXY pressure indication twice.</para></command><comment code="00008910.0001001.004"><para layer="1" lid="N.00008910.0001001.012">A <measure category="Time" show-unit="true" system="SI and derived" unit="min">15</measure> interval must be applied between both checks.</para></comment></action></relevant-sub-proc></procbody></procitem></opsproc>